WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.630
Last week a video went

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.650
round our class group.

3
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.740
A famous footballer promised free

4
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.020
airtime to anyone who shared a link.

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.870
It was fake, and half the class

6
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.070
had already shared it.

7
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.420
Today: how AI fakes are made, why your

8
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.860
eyes aren't enough, and how to check.

9
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.340
A deepfake is a photo, video or voice

10
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.200
made or changed by AI to look real.

11
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.810
Face swapping puts one

12
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.490
face on another body.

13
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.970
Lip-syncing makes a mouth say new words.

14
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.340
And a voice can be copied

15
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.360
from a short clip.

16
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.040
You may know the old clues: odd

17
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.180
hands, blurry teeth, a robot voice.

18
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:46.660
They help sometimes.

19
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.590
But new tools fix them, so a fake with

20
00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.570
no mistakes can still be fake.

21
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.450
You already know three questions: who

22
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.370
made it, where is the original, and do

23
00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.090
trusted sources report it?

24
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.220
Now let's answer them like a fact-checker.

25
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.170
Check the story, not just the picture.

26
00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.170
First, the account: is it new,

27
00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.470
or copying a famous name?

28
00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.150
Second, the original: a reverse image

29
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.250
search shows where a picture appeared

30
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:19.570
first.

31
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.520
Third, a trusted news site

32
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.660
or official page.

33
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.890
Fourth, who gains if you believe it?

34
00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:28.470
Quick check!

35
00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.850
A clip shows our head teacher

36
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:33.170
saying school is closed tomorrow.

37
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.090
It's on a new account with no other posts.

38
00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.510
What do you do?

39
00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.150
Check the real channel first: the

40
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.610
school's notice board, its

41
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:44.710
official page, or your teacher.

42
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.660
A new account with no

43
00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.460
history is a warning sign.

44
00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.990
And forwarding it, even to

45
00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.390
ask, helps it spread.

46
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.300
What about AI detectors?

47
00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.890
Some tools hide a watermark in what they

48
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.570
make, or add an “AI-made” label.

49
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.900
A detector looks for those signs.

50
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.870
But it gives a chance, not

51
00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.770
proof: honest work gets flagged,

52
00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.530
and edits wipe the signal.

53
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.610
In the app, write with a hidden

54
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.170
watermark and watch the detector flag it.

55
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.580
Then change a few words, and

56
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.880
watch the flag disappear.

57
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.590
And notice when an honest

58
00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.450
sentence gets flagged by chance.

59
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:29.530
Some fakes are made to hurt people.

60
00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.330
A fake photo of a classmate

61
00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.730
can spread in minutes.

62
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.300
Making or sharing one is never a joke,

63
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.980
and in many countries it's a crime.

64
00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:42.960
Your turn.

65
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.900
Someone posts a fake picture

66
00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.120
of you in a group chat.

67
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.740
What's the best first step?

68
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.760
Save evidence, report it, and

69
00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.420
tell an adult you trust.

70
00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.130
Remember: glitches don't

71
00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.850
last, so check the story.

72
00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.150
Detectors are clues, not proof.

73
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.380
And never make or share a

74
00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.120
fake of a real person.

75
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.540
Try it tomorrow: pick one picture or clip

76
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.740
going round your family or class group.

77
00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.270
Check the account, search for the

78
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.570
original, and look for a trusted report.

79
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.620
Then tell the group what you found,

80
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.340
kindly, without forwarding it.
